WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.337
This slide demonstrates one of the easiest case
mistakes to make In

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.468
the first query we check whether age is at least
eighteen before

00:00:08.481 --> 00:00:13.754
checking whether age is at least sixty-five A
sixty-five-year-old also satisfies the

00:00:13.766 --> 00:00:18.058
first condition so SQL immediately labels that
person Adult and never reaches

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:23.921
the Senior branch That makes the Senior branch
unreachable In the corrected

00:00:23.947 --> 00:00:28.058
version we place the more specific condition first
age at least sixty-five

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:33.373
followed by age at least eighteen Both versions are
provided in the

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:38.645
code cell Run them in the browser and compare the
results You

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:44.519
can also copy them into pgAdmin Remember when
conditions overlap

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:47.728
put the more specific condition before the broader
condition
